<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of the Peoples of Cameroon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Union des Populations du Cameroun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of the Peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> (UPC) is a Cameroonian political party founded in 1948 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruben-um-nyobe">Ruben Um Nyobe</a>. It demanded independence for French Cameroon and reunification with the British Cameroons. Banned by the French in 1955, it waged an armed insurgency that continued after independence in 1960; Um Nyobe was killed in 1958, and his successor Félix-Roland Moumié was poisoned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> in 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-of-the-peoples-of-cameroon.jpg" alt="Union of the Peoples of Cameroon" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NorthTension · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Union_of_the_Peoples_of_Cameroon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
